\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. A Gladsome hymn of praise we Sing,
\par And thankfully we gather,
\par To bless the love of God above,
\par Our everlasting Father.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In Him rejoice with heart and voice,
\par Whose glory fadeth never,
\par Whose providence is our defence,
\par Who lives and loves for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. From shades of night He calls the light,
\par And from the sod the flower;
\par From every cloud His blessings break,
\par In sunshine or in shower.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In Him rejoice with heart and voice,
\par Whose glory fadeth never,
\par Whose providence is our defence,
\par Who lives and loves for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Full in His sight His children stand,
\par By His strong arm defended;
\par And He whose wisdom guides the world,
\par Our footsteps hath attended.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In Him rejoice with heart and voice,
\par Whose glory fadeth never,
\par Whose providence is our defence,
\par Who lives and loves for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For nothing falls unknown to Him-
\par Or care or joy or sorrow;
\par And He whose mercy ruled the past,
\par Will be our stay to- morrow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In Him rejoice with heart and voice,
\par Whose glory fadeth never,
\par Whose providence is our defence,
\par Who lives and loves for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then praise the Lord with one accord,
\par To His great name give glory,
\par And of His never- changing love
\par Repeat the wondrous story.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par In Him rejoice with heart and voice,
\par Whose glory fadeth never,
\par Whose providence is our defence,
\par Who lives and loves for ever.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

